.TH SXFER 1 "2026-10-05" "sxfer" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sxfer \- high-speed, one-way serial file tree transfer using fast-lzma2, RaptorQ fountain coding, and baseband line coding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sxfer send
.RI [ options ]
.IR PATH ...
.br
.B sxfer recv
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B sxfer crc
.IR FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sxfer
copies complete directory hierarchies and file trees across a one-way (simplex / TX-only) serial link
(such as USB-to-UART, RS-485, optical isolators, or unidirectional data diodes).
There is no reverse channel, no ACKs/NACKs, and no backpressure handshake.
.PP
To ensure maximum throughput, zero transmission gaps, and robust erasure recovery,
.B sxfer
integrates:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBMulti-Threaded fast-lzma2 Compression\fR: Parallel multithreaded dictionary compression.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRateless Fountain Coding (RFC 6330 RaptorQ / Systematic Codes over GF(256))\fR: Files are partitioned into source blocks of up to 128 symbols. Systematic symbols are transmitted with zero overhead, followed by an endless stream of independent repair symbols. Receiving any (1 + \(*e) symbols allows complete reconstruction via full-pivoting Gaussian elimination over GF(256).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBBaud-Adaptive Dynamic Chunk Sizing\fR: Chunks scale dynamically with baud rate (1 KiB for <500k baud, 4 KiB for 500k\(en2.5M baud, and 16 KiB for \(>=2.5M baud) to minimize kernel context switch overhead.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBContinuous 3-Stage Streaming Pipeline\fR: Disk reader/compressor, RaptorQ fountain encoder, and 64 KiB batched zero-copy serial TX operate concurrently with thread-safe ring buffering, saturating UART TX FIFOs at 100%.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBBaseband Line Coding & Framing\fR: Consistent Overhead Byte Stuffing (COBS) with 0x00 frame boundaries and Galois LFSR whitening to prevent bit stuffing loss and clock drift.
.PP
.B sxfer send
walks each
.IR PATH ,
compresses files using fast-lzma2, encodes fountain symbols, and streams frames through the pipeline.
Paths are transmitted relative to the working directory.
.PP
.B sxfer recv
runs on the receiving machine and should be started before the sender.
It reconstructs files, verifies 32-bit CRC checksums, and applies directory hierarchies, permissions, timestamps, and symlinks.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS send
.TP
.BI \-d " DEV"
Serial device or output file/FIFO (default
.BR /dev/ttyUSB0 ).
.TP
.BI \-b " BAUD"
Baud rate from 1200 up to 4000000+ (default
.BR 115200 ).
.TP
.BI \-m " MODE"
Framing and line coding modulation:
.B cobs
(Consistent Overhead Byte Stuffing with 0x00 delimiter, recommended),
.B scramble
(Galois LFSR data whitener with magic sync prefix), or
.B raw
(standard sync marker with length header). Default is
.BR cobs .
.TP
.BI \-w " DIR"
Watch directory mode: automatically creates \fIDIR\fR if not existed, continuously monitors it for incoming files or directory trees, transmits them over the serial line with RaptorQ protection, and deletes them upon successful transfer.
.TP
.BI \-c " BYTES"

Symbol chunk size in bytes (16 to 65536). If omitted or 0, chunk size is chosen adaptively based on baud rate.
.TP
.BI \-f " PCT"
Extra RaptorQ fountain repair symbols to generate as a percentage of source symbols (default
.BR 20 ).
.TP
.BI \-r " ROUNDS"
Number of transmission rounds (default
.BR 2 ).
.TP
.BI \-z " LEVEL"
fast-lzma2 compression level:
.B 0
for uncompressed,
.B 1\(en9
for fast-lzma2 dictionary levels (default
.BR 6 ).
.TP
.BI \-l " FILE"
Append timestamped log entries to
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B \-h
Display help summary.
.SS recv
.TP
.BI \-d " DEV"
Serial device or input FIFO (default
.BR /dev/ttyUSB0 ).
.TP
.BI \-b " BAUD"
Baud rate (default
.BR 115200 ).
.TP
.BI \-m " MODE"
Demodulation / framing mode:
.BR cobs ,
.BR scramble ,
or
.B raw
(default
.BR cobs ).
.TP
.BI \-o " DIR"
Destination directory for received files (default
.BR ./recv ).
.TP
.BI \-q " SEC"
Quit after
.I SEC
seconds of line silence.
.TP
.B \-p
Restore original file owner and group (requires root).
.TP
.BI \-l " FILE"
Append timestamped log entries to
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B \-h
Display help summary.
.SS crc
.TP
.B sxfer crc \fIFILE\fR
Compute and print the standard IEEE 802.3 CRC-32 checksum of
.IR FILE .
.SH RECOVERY & VERIFICATION
.TP
.B RaptorQ Rateless Fountain Coding
Files are divided into source blocks with K <= 128 symbols.
The receiver accumulates incoming symbols and performs Gaussian elimination over GF(256) as soon as K independent symbols are received.
Packet drops during transmission do not require retransmission; any subsequent repair symbol replaces any lost source symbol.
.TP
.B Frame Checking
Each transmitted frame contains a dedicated 32-bit CRC covering the packet contents. Corrupted frames caused by electrical noise are dropped immediately before reaching the decoder.
.TP
.B File Integrity
The end-to-end CRC-32 of every source file is verified upon reassembly and decompression prior to final atomic renaming.
.SH EXAMPLES
Send a directory tree over a 2.5 Mbaud RS-485 line with fast-lzma2 level 6 and COBS framing:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sxfer send -d /dev/ttyUSB0 -b 2500000 -m cobs -z 6 -r 2 src/ assets/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Receive the files into
.IR /opt/data :
.PP
.RS
.nf
sxfer recv -d /dev/ttyUSB0 -b 2500000 -m cobs -o /opt/data -q 10
.fi
.RE
.PP
Test transfers over an IPC named pipe:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mkfifo /tmp/wire
sxfer recv -d /tmp/wire -o /tmp/dst -q 2 &
sxfer send -d /tmp/wire -m cobs -f 30 file1.bin dir2/
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR termios (3),
.BR stty (1)